{"id":"n-20261023-o2qxb2","category":"finance","display_title":"Bill Ackman Praises Israeli Economy","display_title_he":"ביל אקמן מהלל את הכלכלה הישראלית","short_summary":"Billionaire investor Bill Ackman expressed immense optimism about Israel's economic future during a recent visit, highlighting its intellectual capital and potential in the age of artificial intelligence.","english_level":"C1","words":446,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001560519","title":"המיליארדר ביל אקמן: \"ישראל תהיה אחת הכלכלות הטובות בעולם\"","published_at":"2026-10-22T14:16:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-22T14:16:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-23T06:23:39.369Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Billionaire investor Bill Ackman recently shared an exceptionally optimistic outlook regarding the Israeli economy, predicting it will become one of the strongest globally. Speaking at the Summit ARC conference hosted by Sheba Medical Center's Director General, Prof. Yitzhak Kreiss, Ackman revealed that he and his wife, designer and researcher Neri Oxman, purchased a five percent stake in the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange shortly after the events of October 7. According to the investor, that swift decision reflected his unwavering belief in the resilience of Israeli capitalism and his absolute trust in the country's future.","Addressing Israel's economic comparative advantages in the era of artificial intelligence, Ackman argued that the country's traditionally perceived disadvantage—its small population size—could actually transform into a major asset. While larger nations like the United States and France struggle with massive national debts driven by large populations, Israel possesses the highest concentration of intelligence quotient and intellectual property per capita. He noted that as Israeli entrepreneurs increasingly choose to scale and sell companies at later stages rather than exiting early, a small population means fewer people will share the massive wealth generated by future billion-dollar corporations.","On the geopolitical front, Ackman expressed support for Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, stating that he defended the nation effectively during wartime and helped reset the Middle East, thereby reducing regional risk and improving prospects for peace. Furthermore, he noted that the current American president is eager to resolve the situation, views Iran as a major risk, and is free from future election pressures. Conversely, Ackman voiced strict concerns regarding the rise of social democracy in the United States, which he believes poses a direct threat to both capitalism and Israel.","Beyond finance, Ackman discussed a profound personal turning point that led him to establish the AOI institute for brain health and longevity. Following a frightening medical emergency in which his younger daughter Lucy suffered a brain hemorrhage from a ruptured blood vessel, Ackman dedicated his time to navigating her complex recovery and establishing a major medical center. Although he acknowledged that the elite medical resources he secured are not accessible to the general public, the ordeal reinforced his critical view of bureaucratic inefficiencies, poor incentives, and the lack of preventive medicine in traditional healthcare systems.","Highlighting the transformative power of modern technology, Ackman revealed that his family consults artificial intelligence tools daily to assist with medical decisions, drug interactions, and treatment strategies for his daughter's rehabilitation. Concluding with a broader philosophical perspective, Ackman maintained that human life today is vastly superior to past centuries, driven by rapid advancements in artificial intelligence, upcoming breakthroughs in understanding human cognition, and powerful tools that will soon cure many diseases."],"facts":[{"fact":"Billionaire investor Bill Ackman stated during the Summit ARC conference at Sheba Medical Center that Israel will be one of the best economies in the world.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Ackman and his wife Neri Oxman acquired a 5% stake in the Tel Aviv Stock Exchange shortly after October 7, expressing strong confidence in Israeli capitalism.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Ackman noted that while Israel's small population can be a disadvantage traditionally, it becomes an asset in the age of AI because the country boasts exceptionally high IQ and IP per capita.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Following a medical emergency involving his younger daughter Lucy, who suffered a brain hemorrhage, Ackman established the AOI institute focused on brain health and longevity.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Ackman praised Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu for defending the country well during the war and noted that geopolitical risks in the Middle East have decreased.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Ackman mentioned utilizing artificial intelligence tools like Claude daily to consult on medical decisions regarding his daughter's treatment and recovery.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Billionaire","lemma":"billionaire","pos":"noun","he":"מיליארדר","name":"Billionaire"},{"text":"investor","lemma":"investor","pos":"noun","he":"משקיע","name":false},{"text":"Bill Ackman","lemma":"Bill Ackman","pos":"proper noun","he":"ביל אקמן","name":"Bill Ackman"},{"text":"recently","lemma":"recently","pos":"adverb","he":"לאחרונה","name":false},{"text":"shared","lemma":"share","pos":"verb","he":"שיתף","name":false},{"text":"optimistic","lemma":"optimistic","pos":"adjective","he":"אופטימי","name":false},{"text":"outlook","lemma":"outlook","pos":"noun","he":"השקפה / תחזית","name":false},{"text":"regarding","lemma":"regard","pos":"preposition","he":"בנוגע ל-","name":false},{"text":"Israeli","lemma":"Israeli","pos":"adjective","he":"ישראלי","name":"Israeli"},{"text":"economy","lemma":"eco